%% Memory Tax: net value of agent memory vs naive RAG, with the three tax sources — [Conceptual reconstruction]
flowchart TD
    H["Raw interaction history H"] --> CH["Naive RAG: turn chunks, BM25 + dense, rerank"]
    H --> I["Memory ingestion I(H): LLM extract / summarise / link"]
    I --> M["Memory store M"]
    Q["Query q"] --> CH
    Q --> R["Memory retrieval R(q, M)"]
    M --> R
    CH --> G1["QA backbone G(q, C_rag)"]
    R --> G2["QA backbone G(q, C_mem)"]
    G1 --> J["LLM judge per query"]
    G2 --> J
    J --> BEN["Benefit: memory right, RAG wrong"]
    J --> TAX["Tax: RAG right, memory wrong"]
    BEN --> NV["Net value = Benefit - Tax"]
    TAX --> NV
    I -. "Faithfulness loss (Fig. 3, Table 2)" .-> TAX
    R -. "Accessibility loss (Fig. 4, Fig. 5)" .-> TAX
    G2 -. "Robustness loss (Fig. 6)" .-> TAX
